    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d206">

                <pb facs="0261" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.51 Frozen Credits 35/316a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-04T20:00:00-04:00">February 4, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>210. The Department is still considering the status of the two banks in
                        Argentina<anchor n="43" xml:id="d206-f1"/> as outlined in your No. 302,
                    February 2, 5 p.m.,<anchor n="44" xml:id="d206-f2"/> but does not contemplate
                    action pending further developments in Argentina.</p>
                <p>Department is confident, in this connection, that you will report promptly any
                    measures to implement decree severing financial transactions with Axis and any
                    action taken by the Argentine Government to control financial transactions
                    within Argentina which may be of benefit to Axis nationals.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d206-f1" n="43" xml:id="d206-f1-content">
                <p>Banco de la Nación and Banco de la Provincia Buenos Aires.</p>
